cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Interactive Math Teaching Tools"
abstract: >-
  A collection of 40+ real-time, browser-based web applications for teaching
  and learning Differential Equations, Linear Algebra, and Numerical Methods.
  Includes phase portraits, linear algebra calculators, mass-spring-damping
  systems, polynomial interpolation, finite difference schemes, and more.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kapita
    given-names: Shelvean
    name-suffix: Ph.D.
repository-code: "https://github.com/shelvean/math-tools"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - education
  - interactive
  - differential-equations
  - linear-algebra
  - numerical-methods
  - visualization
  - teaching
